Ladybird gives a rendered legend its fit-content inline size, applies
the inline-size limits, and resolves auto margins against the result.
The limits also apply to its intrinsic contribution to the fieldset.

Blink lays out the legend in FieldsetLayoutAlgorithm::LayoutLegend(),
using CreateConstraintSpaceForLegend() to supply its available size and
percentage basis. Gecko reflows the legend in nsFieldSetFrame::Reflow().
WebKit lays out the legend in RenderBlock::layoutExcludedChildren().

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all clamped a
legend with 4px of padding and a 20px maximum content width to 24px.
They agreed on minimum and percentage limits, vertical writing,
intrinsic fieldsets, and child widths after the maximum changed.
